onboarding.hookSetupPrompt:
Please set up {{product}}'s notification hooks. Only two events are needed: Stop (the notification text) and PostToolUse (matcher: AskUserQuestion, the name of the tool that asked). Session status (running / done / waiting for input) comes from herdr, so it needs no hook.
Hook command: {{command}}
The config file is ~/.claude/settings.json for Claude Code and ~/.codex/hooks.json for Codex; both take the same shape (use hooks.json for Codex — writing these into config.toml makes Codex warn):
{"hooks":{"Stop":[{"hooks":[{"type":"command","command":"{{command}}"}]}],"PostToolUse":[{"matcher":"AskUserQuestion","hooks":[{"type":"command","command":"{{command}}"}]}]}}
Merge this into the existing file. Do not overwrite other settings or existing hook entries — add {{command}} as a new entry, or append to the existing hooks array.
PreToolUse and UserPromptSubmit are not needed (harmless if already registered — leave them alone). Grok Build reads Claude's settings.json, so it needs no separate config.
